ality-of-the-unseelie?p=1410900#post1410900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> No, Always repay a debt. Means that. Litterally. Functionally Seelie should have many problems with being LAWFUL while the Unseelie should have Chaotic issues. These don't work out and some of the older stuff had silly thing but... those got retconned hard with c20 the unseelie court is a legitimate thing not.. the 5th column.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. And I like it that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-28T18:39:48-07:00","id":1410917,"title":"","content":"Pour L\u2019Amour et Liberte<br /> <br /> For Love and Freedom<br /> <br /> The Unseelie believe in love same as the Seelie do. Just a different kind of love. Rory Gilmore on Gilmore Girls throwing caution to the wind and sleeping with her crush even though he has a fianc\u00e9e because she loves him that much...that\u2019s Unseelie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-30T07:29:54-07:00","id":1411070,"title":"","content":"Yeah that\u2019s what their supose to be, but then they ravage all the time,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-30T16:36:16-07:00","id":1411132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1410859-i-am-confused-about-the-mortality-of-the-unseelie?p=1411070#post1411070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah that\u2019s what their supose to be, but then they ravage all the time,</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ravaging's morality is in the eye of the beholder. Crushing someone's dream of say mass murder is probably a good thing. And getting someone to be less codependent in their dreams of love also is a thing. But really Ravaging can be just.. trolling people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-30T21:36:22-07:00","id":1411166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1410859-i-am-confused-about-the-mortality-of-the-unseelie?p=1411132#post1411132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Ravaging's morality is in the eye of the beholder. Crushing someone's dream of say mass murder is probably a good thing. And getting someone to be less codependent in their dreams of love also is a thing. But really Ravaging can be just.. trolling people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or less dependent on chasing a guy who\u2019s already taken and can\u2019t give them what they really want even if he wanted to? Could Ravaging cure that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-31T15:05:36-07:00","id":1411254,"title":"","content":"I think the best way to understand the morality of the Unseelie (or the Seelie for that matter) is to step back from the Changeling books and go back to the original source material - the folklore about fairies (which is not the same as fairy tales which are told for entertainment, but the actual beliefs of people about the fairies - so you won't necessarily find certain things in fairy tales, but you can find them elsewhere). I think there are two general categories that you can base Unseelie morality on.<br /> <br /> The first are the outright dangerous fairies which kill or harm people, or are given attributes of dangerous natural phenomenon where people could hurt themselves. In these cases, the unseelie represent the dangerous side of nature, and the people they victimize tempt fate by transgressing certain boundaries that common sense, wisdom, or religious taboos would tell you not to do. In this sense, the Unseelie can be seen as a kind of &quot;wrathful deities&quot; that punish people for transgressing certain natural laws. This would be things like &quot;don't wander at night by yourself&quot; (any number of night creatures that eat you), &quot;avoid going out when there is bad weather&quot; (the Wild Hunt will kill you), &quot;children should stay away from bodies of water&quot; (any number of fairies who steal or kill children), or &quot;be wary of members of the opposite sex who are too passionate and wild&quot; (any number of fairy lovers who kill like the leanan sidhe)<br /> <br /> The second are stories where the fairies punish people for moral failings, but which they may also perform because the moral rules don't apply to the fairy. It's very similar to the first, but the source of failing is different. In the first, it's mainly the dangers of the natural world. In the second, its punishment for moral failing of obeying society's conventions. Fairies don't like people who aren't polite, who aren't thankful when given help, who are rude or insulting, who are boastful or too proud, etc. Very similar to the stories of the gods in Greek myths and others. Seelie fairies usually just stop helping such people, or help their enemies instead. Unseelie actively punish such people. In short, the Unseelie don't see undesirable qualities to themselves, but always see such undesirable traits on others and get vindictive as a result. Mapping to Changeling, this would be an insistence that the Unseelie be free and not bound to restrictions. Such fairies can have attractive qualities, but this doesn't always end up good for others (for example, an unseelie might be very generous to others, but don't care that others may not want the &quot;gifts&quot; they provide, or become upset if the other person doesn't respond with the gratitude they think they should receive).<br /> <br /> The Unseelie should not be the same as fairies who ally with the Fomorians. That should still be a distinct (and probably secret) minority. And I think even some Seelie fairies should fall under the Fomorians grasp. It's just more likely the Unseelie are more likely to be so tempted. Some of the sourcebooks probably emphasized the connection too much. If I remember right, originally in the corebook the Shadow Court was simply the Unseelie's &quot;shadow cabinet&quot; who wanted to restore the cycle of leadership. But when the Shadow Court sourcebook came out, it was really about a secret faction of Fomorian allies. That went too far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-31T15:46:37-07:00","id":1411263,"title":"","content":"They changed the Shadow Court in C20 to make them more like anarchists who want to overthrow the old feudal system personified by both the Seelie and Unseelie Courts. They also received a tiebreaking chair in the Parliament of Dreams as a sign of approval from the Dreaming itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-01T20:56:53-07:00","id":1411465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1410859-i-am-confused-about-the-mortality-of-the-unseelie?p=1411166#post1411166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or less dependent on chasing a guy who\u2019s already taken and can\u2019t give them what they really want even if he wanted to? Could Ravaging cure that?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> IT depends on the Ravager. the C20 player's guide did add Unseelie Musing and Seelie ravaging Thresholds. The difference between Ravaging someone of their love and testing it an Musing it aren't going to look very different and the Unseelie following the path is probably going to if they want to claim teh moral high ground talk about how &quot;Love doesn't matter unless its tested&quot; but he gains glamour if you fail or lose the test is all that matters to him.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile Seelie Ravaging can be about taking away self determination.. just go with the group, just keep doing what other people do.. whether this is inspiring an emotion or forcing a life is.. in the eye of the beholder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-02T08:57:06-07:00","id":1411511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1410859-i-am-confused-about-the-mortality-of-the-unseelie?p=1410894#post1410894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Theoretically the Unseelie promote change, individuality over society and so on. Like most things in the WOD they often fail to live up to their ideal. They don't have to work with the Shadow Court(and may not even know it exists) they don't have to be friends with Thallain(or Nephandi, or Sabbat or BSDs). The Seelie are the ones bound to &amp;quot;Have tos&amp;quot; they have pay back debts.. even if the person is a monster. They have to be honorable... even if its hurts more people.. they have to accept things.</div> </div> </div> </div>I barely see any of them prompting Freedom and passion, at least for Humans, they mostly want freedom to hurt other people and get away with ravaging which is clearly emotional abuse, kind of like Marquis de Sade, that man seems like a Unseelie dreamer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-02T13:32:45-07:00","id":1411545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1410859-i-am-confused-about-the-mortality-of-the-unseelie?p=1411511#post1411511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I barely see any of them prompting Freedom and passion, at least for Humans, they mostly want freedom to hurt other people and get away with ravaging which is clearly emotional abuse, kind of like Marquis de Sade, that man seems like a Unseelie dreamer.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The difference between testing someone's emotion and them coming out stronger for it and showing they &quot;really didn't love anyone&quot; isn't going to look much different. If you are saying &quot;The Unseelie are bad from human morality sense&quot;.. They are fairies. They have prorities that are not &quot;for the good fo humanity&quot; There's one group in the WOD that prioritizes Humanity's good over all other things.<br /> <br /> Its called The Technocracy. They believe nature should be tamed, Dreams should be bent and Gods should be killed. Horror is the price of Wonder. Faries are by their nature horrific the idea that musing isn't good for a person any more than farming is good for a cow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}